  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nHigh pressure will continue to provide dry conditions across the \narea. Another chilly night on tap with dry air mass in place and \nlight winds. Issued a frost advisory for locations most susceptible \nto frost late tonight, i.e. SE Ohio and north central WV. Outside of \nthe advisory patchy frost is still possible in sheltered valleys. \n\nFog can also be expected again most mornings this week in favored \nriver valleys. \n\nWith the dry air mass in place, afternoon RH values will continue to \ndrop into the 30 percent range for much of the area. Winds will \nhowever remain light, owing for fire danger to remain relatively low \noverall.",
